* **Nominal State:** The primary THz excitation oscillator runs at a baseline resonance of $3.435\text{ THz}$, while the secondary Phase-Locked Loop (PLL) stabilization oscillator runs at $15.3435\text{ MHz}$.[1]
* **Emergency Throttle:** When the engine enters a high-load or thermal-drift state, the driver applies a phase-shift ($\Delta f$) to the secondary $15.3435\text{ MHz}$ PLL oscillator.[1] This dampens the harmonic acoustic vibrations in the Lu-Bi matrix [1], protecting the crystalline lattice from structural collapse or reaching its Born-melting temperature of $1319.82\text{ K}$ ($1046.67^\circ\text{C}$).

## 2. Telemetry-Bandwidth Hysteresis
To ensure zero data loss during computational mode transitions (between standard and high-precision modes), the telemetry buffer implements a hardware-level hysteresis gate.

| Engine State | Buffer Depth | Sampling Rate | Fidelity Mode |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| FAST | 1024 packets | 1 MHz | Standard |
| PRECISE | 16384 packets | 10 MHz | High-Fidelity |

### 2.1 Transition Dynamics
When `SnijdersOmegaEngineV128` triggers the `PRECISE` mode, the hardware trigger line forces the telemetry buffer to scale from 1024 to 16384 packets within $t < 5\mu\text{s}$. This accommodates the high-fidelity 70-decimal data stream without generating buffer overflows or packet loss under extreme space radiation conditions.
